  "statement": "Given that $\\log_{2}3=a$ and $\\log_{3}5=b$, express $\\log_{5}2$ in terms of $a$ and $b$.",
  "solution": "By the change-of-base formula, $\\log_{2}5=\\log_{2}3\\cdot\\log_{3}5=ab$. Therefore $\\log_{5}2=\\dfrac{1}{\\log_{2}5}=\\dfrac{1}{ab}$.",
